WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.491 --> 00:00:01.536
- Hello everyone.

00:00:01.536 --> 00:00:04.238
Welcome to another
episode of Unlocking Lily.

00:00:04.238 --> 00:00:06.919
It's always been my dream to be a speaker,

00:00:06.919 --> 00:00:10.455
where I can inspire people
to do extraordinary things.

00:00:10.455 --> 00:00:14.622
A few months ago I decided to
make a life altering decision.

00:00:15.677 --> 00:00:19.177
I quit my day job to pursue this full time

00:00:20.788 --> 00:00:24.955
and you guys are all coming
along for the ride with me.

00:00:28.123 --> 00:00:30.191
Every challenge that I take on

00:00:30.191 --> 00:00:33.075
is to help me grow as a speaker.

00:00:33.075 --> 00:00:36.387
My challenge this time
is my first corporate gig

00:00:36.387 --> 00:00:40.562
with Sage Summit, which is a
two day business conference.

00:00:40.562 --> 00:00:43.134
I'll be taking part in the Mentor Lounge,

00:00:43.134 --> 00:00:46.244
where people can come in
and book one on one coaching

00:00:46.244 --> 00:00:49.016
with me and talk about two specific areas.

00:00:49.016 --> 00:00:51.564
The first area is leadership and vision,

00:00:51.564 --> 00:00:55.282
and the second one is
attracting and retaining talent.

00:00:55.282 --> 00:00:58.296
When Evan surprised me
with this opportunity

00:00:58.296 --> 00:01:01.894
to be part of Sage Summit I
was so incredibly excited.

00:01:01.894 --> 00:01:04.516
I was like, "Yes, this
is exactly what I want."

00:01:04.516 --> 00:01:07.259
I am so so grateful for this opportunity.

00:01:07.259 --> 00:01:09.758
And then I started to think,

00:01:09.758 --> 00:01:12.675
oh, I actually have to go out there

00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:18.027
and be courageous and show up

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:23.168
and answer peoples' questions
and be someone's mentor.

00:01:23.168 --> 00:01:26.835
What if I go there and
I sit there by myself

00:01:28.336 --> 00:01:31.169
and no one shows up to talk to me?

00:01:32.676 --> 00:01:36.162
How am I going to deal
with that rejection?

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:39.909
What if everybody wants to talk to me

00:01:39.909 --> 00:01:42.076
and I have nothing to say?

00:01:44.227 --> 00:01:45.793
What if people ask me questions

00:01:45.793 --> 00:01:48.720
that are way above my head and I

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:51.663
completely make a fool out of myself?

00:01:51.663 --> 00:01:52.496
What then?

00:01:53.918 --> 00:01:56.126
And then that's when I was like,
no, no, this is ridiculous.

00:01:56.126 --> 00:01:58.594
I need to stop thinking like this.

00:01:58.594 --> 00:02:03.105
Obviously Evan recommended
me, because he believed

00:02:03.105 --> 00:02:06.252
I am qualified and capable to do this.

00:02:06.252 --> 00:02:07.950
Amazing, great.

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:10.283
Well what if I let him down?

00:02:12.278 --> 00:02:14.368
It's his name on the line here.

00:02:14.368 --> 00:02:15.768
He vouched for me.

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:17.415
I have to perform well.

00:02:17.415 --> 00:02:21.332
What if I fall flat on
my face and now he feels

00:02:22.505 --> 00:02:26.053
like he made a mistake in recommending me?

00:02:26.053 --> 00:02:28.326
What do I do then?

00:02:28.326 --> 00:02:29.563
That's when I thought about something

00:02:29.563 --> 00:02:32.445
that was quite interesting about me.

00:02:32.445 --> 00:02:35.262
All my life I never feel that I'm worthy

00:02:35.262 --> 00:02:37.717
of the things that happen to me.

00:02:37.717 --> 00:02:39.698
I lean into the gratitude a lot.

00:02:39.698 --> 00:02:43.629
I'm so grateful for Evan, for
giving me the opportunity.

00:02:43.629 --> 00:02:46.403
I'm so grateful for all
of you for supporting me,

00:02:46.403 --> 00:02:49.572
but I never give myself credit

00:02:49.572 --> 00:02:51.671
that I have worked hard for something,

00:02:51.671 --> 00:02:54.766
that I do deserve it and am worthy.

00:02:54.766 --> 00:02:56.673
And that's when I thought, you know what

00:02:56.673 --> 00:03:00.708
I need to really change
my mindset around it.

00:03:00.708 --> 00:03:03.909
Yes, of course I'm new,
and yes I'm very grateful

00:03:03.909 --> 00:03:06.548
for all the opportunities
that are coming my way,

00:03:06.548 --> 00:03:10.205
and it wouldn't happen unless
Evan was helping me out.

00:03:10.205 --> 00:03:14.332
But at the same time,
my intention is pure.

00:03:14.332 --> 00:03:18.372
My intention is to add as
much value as possible.

00:03:18.372 --> 00:03:21.934
My mission is to help
people become extraordinary.

00:03:21.934 --> 00:03:24.037
As long as I keep that in mind

00:03:24.037 --> 00:03:27.663
and work really hard to prepare
myself to show up and say,

00:03:27.663 --> 00:03:29.946
"Hey, you know, I am
qualified to do this."

00:03:29.946 --> 00:03:32.269
And I am ready and prepared

00:03:32.269 --> 00:03:34.890
and I've spent the last couple of weeks

00:03:34.890 --> 00:03:39.063
really really preparing and
getting ready for this event.

00:03:39.063 --> 00:03:42.385
Then if things do kind of go wrong,

00:03:42.385 --> 00:03:44.702
which it will, things are never perfect,

00:03:44.702 --> 00:03:46.942
I can learn from those mistakes

00:03:46.942 --> 00:03:49.336
and I can use this as an experience

00:03:49.336 --> 00:03:53.503
as long as I know that my
intention is to help others.

00:03:53.503 --> 00:03:55.566
My intention's about the mentees

00:03:55.566 --> 00:03:56.997
that are going to be coming in.

00:03:56.997 --> 00:03:59.389
It's not about me freaking
out and being panicky.

00:03:59.389 --> 00:04:01.905
If I'm panicking, they're
going to be panicking too.

00:04:01.905 --> 00:04:05.223
It's my job to stay calm and provide them

00:04:05.223 --> 00:04:08.670
with a great experience, and know that

00:04:08.670 --> 00:04:11.340
this is why I'm doing
this in the first place.

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:13.290
So when I thought about all of that

00:04:13.290 --> 00:04:16.229
it immediately gave me the excitement,

00:04:16.229 --> 00:04:19.612
which was great, and also the confidence

00:04:19.612 --> 00:04:22.873
to go and continue on and feel great

00:04:22.873 --> 00:04:26.452
that I'm not only incredibly lucky

00:04:26.452 --> 00:04:29.974
to be given this opportunity,
I also deserve it,

00:04:29.974 --> 00:04:32.319
because I've been working
so incredibly hard

00:04:32.319 --> 00:04:34.197
towards this goal.

00:04:34.197 --> 00:04:36.197
I'm so excited for this.

00:04:37.702 --> 00:04:38.799
Good morning everyone.

00:04:38.799 --> 00:04:41.481
Today is actually the big day.

00:04:41.481 --> 00:04:43.398
It's about 5, 5:15 a.m.

00:04:46.492 --> 00:04:48.290
I'm an early morning riser.

00:04:48.290 --> 00:04:50.667
This is amazing for me.

00:04:50.667 --> 00:04:53.227
This is like the best
time of the day for me,

00:04:53.227 --> 00:04:56.727
where I can reflect and start my day right

00:04:58.681 --> 00:05:01.238
and see what are the
things that I need to do.

00:05:01.238 --> 00:05:04.956
The first thing that I do,
after I get dressed and shower

00:05:04.956 --> 00:05:09.732
and everything, is actually
do a walking meditation.

00:05:09.732 --> 00:05:13.899
What that is is that I look
at the environment around me

00:05:15.248 --> 00:05:17.748
and just focus on that.

00:05:17.748 --> 00:05:21.915
For example, if I were just
to look at these trees,

00:05:23.081 --> 00:05:26.414
for example, I just focus on the leaves.

00:05:27.436 --> 00:05:29.186
I focus on the color.

00:05:30.910 --> 00:05:33.839
I don't think about
anything else but that.

00:05:33.839 --> 00:05:37.770
So I'm going to do that quickly,
for about five minutes or so

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:40.437
and then I'll see you very soon.

00:05:42.233 --> 00:05:44.816
(upbeat music)

00:05:51.271 --> 00:05:53.080
I finally ended up in
the exhibition grounds

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:55.203
where the Sage Summit is taking place.

00:05:55.203 --> 00:05:56.957
So I'm just following the crowd

00:05:56.957 --> 00:05:58.859
and hopefully I'm going to find it.

00:05:58.859 --> 00:05:59.822
And whoever's ahead of me,

00:05:59.822 --> 00:06:01.529
hopefully they're going
in the right direction,

00:06:01.529 --> 00:06:03.247
and then meet up with Evan very very soon.

00:06:03.247 --> 00:06:05.580
He's here already; so early.

00:06:07.437 --> 00:06:10.715
I got my badge and I see Evan.

00:06:10.715 --> 00:06:11.965
This is so weird.

00:06:11.965 --> 00:06:13.502
This is so meta.

00:06:13.502 --> 00:06:15.361
Look who it is.

00:06:15.361 --> 00:06:17.156
- [Evan] It's Lily, she's filming.

00:06:17.156 --> 00:06:18.456
Look at this.

00:06:18.456 --> 00:06:19.733
Yours says New to Sage, look at that.

00:06:19.733 --> 00:06:20.566
- Yeah

00:06:20.566 --> 00:06:21.399
- All right.

00:06:21.399 --> 00:06:22.557
- Maybe people will be nicer to me.

00:06:22.557 --> 00:06:24.290
(laughing)

00:06:24.290 --> 00:06:26.042
We're going to head inside soon.

00:06:26.042 --> 00:06:28.625
(upbeat music)

00:06:29.872 --> 00:06:33.254
I got out of two back to
back mentoring sessions.

00:06:33.254 --> 00:06:36.150
I think, overall, it went really well.

00:06:36.150 --> 00:06:38.784
People left really happy.

00:06:38.784 --> 00:06:40.927
With the first one I feel like

00:06:40.927 --> 00:06:45.153
I could have done more
with his limiting beliefs.

00:06:45.153 --> 00:06:47.391
I could have dug a little deeper.

00:06:47.391 --> 00:06:50.808
Given the situation, I kind of hesitated.

00:06:52.315 --> 00:06:54.401
Any time I hesitate I don't end up

00:06:54.401 --> 00:06:57.161
following through the way I want.

00:06:57.161 --> 00:06:59.291
I still think he left with tons of value,

00:06:59.291 --> 00:07:02.958
but he didn't actually
get to the real issue

00:07:04.432 --> 00:07:07.736
that he was facing, so I
definitely needed to change that.

00:07:07.736 --> 00:07:10.099
And then the second one, I was able to

00:07:10.099 --> 00:07:12.138
take the immediate
feedback that I gave myself

00:07:12.138 --> 00:07:16.056
and I started asking more
important questions right away,

00:07:16.056 --> 00:07:18.034
so that way I could get to
the solution a lot faster.

00:07:18.034 --> 00:07:20.506
I think I still could have

00:07:20.506 --> 00:07:22.881
gone a little bit faster than I did.

00:07:22.881 --> 00:07:27.319
Better, better, but I
could have been faster

00:07:27.319 --> 00:07:30.409
and I could have helped him
a lot more with a solution,

00:07:30.409 --> 00:07:32.348
and helping his business and how to

00:07:32.348 --> 00:07:35.956
create his messaging around
what's important to him,

00:07:35.956 --> 00:07:38.778
but in the end, what made me really happy

00:07:38.778 --> 00:07:40.485
is he left and he says,

00:07:40.485 --> 00:07:42.586
"I'm going to start doing this right now.

00:07:42.586 --> 00:07:44.203
"It's going to be this afternoon,

00:07:44.203 --> 00:07:47.860
and thank you for helping
me take immediate action",

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:51.165
and that, to me, is the biggest thank you

00:07:51.165 --> 00:07:52.432
someone could give me.

00:07:52.432 --> 00:07:54.029
So I feel really good.

00:07:54.029 --> 00:07:56.116
Tomorrow I'm back at this again

00:07:56.116 --> 00:07:57.839
and I'm going to try to find ways

00:07:57.839 --> 00:08:02.006
to get to the problem a lot
faster than I have been.

00:08:02.911 --> 00:08:06.187
And that's been an
ongoing progress for me.

00:08:06.187 --> 00:08:08.218
I'm really excited for
tomorrow, but super pumped

00:08:08.218 --> 00:08:11.875
about the two mentees that I had today.

00:08:11.875 --> 00:08:12.708
Okay, bye.

00:08:16.171 --> 00:08:18.838
Today is day two of Sage Summit.

00:08:21.171 --> 00:08:24.950
I was just thinking about
the two mentoring sessions

00:08:24.950 --> 00:08:29.117
that I had, this morning and
how much joy that brought me.

00:08:30.283 --> 00:08:33.708
I always approach any
kind of mentoring session

00:08:33.708 --> 00:08:37.671
or coaching session with
a lot of nervousness,

00:08:37.671 --> 00:08:42.517
because I'm always worried that
I'm not adding enough value.

00:08:42.517 --> 00:08:45.582
What are the things
that I could do better?

00:08:45.582 --> 00:08:48.549
And then once I have
the person face to face,

00:08:48.549 --> 00:08:50.854
everything else just kind of fades

00:08:50.854 --> 00:08:54.982
and I just focus on them and
the things that they can do

00:08:54.982 --> 00:08:57.603
to inspire themselves.

00:08:57.603 --> 00:09:01.451
So really thinking about the
two people that I had yesterday

00:09:01.451 --> 00:09:03.798
and how happy they were when they left

00:09:03.798 --> 00:09:05.827
and how they're going to
take immediate action;

00:09:05.827 --> 00:09:08.201
I actually received an
email from one of them

00:09:08.201 --> 00:09:12.368
saying that his day went
from a 7 and 1/2 to a 11

00:09:14.005 --> 00:09:16.781
and he wanted to thank me for that.

00:09:16.781 --> 00:09:19.698
So all of that makes it so worth it

00:09:21.139 --> 00:09:23.889
to wake up at 4:45 in the morning

00:09:25.789 --> 00:09:28.606
to get down there and to
do the mentoring session.

00:09:28.606 --> 00:09:31.939
I don't know, that's why I do what I do.

00:09:35.538 --> 00:09:37.888
It's to see other people happy.

00:09:37.888 --> 00:09:39.821
It's to see them getting inspired.

00:09:39.821 --> 00:09:43.539
It's to see them taking action right away,

00:09:43.539 --> 00:09:46.831
whether if it's in their life or business

00:09:46.831 --> 00:09:49.540
or relationships, whatever
it is that they need.

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:53.170
And I'm going to just take
that with me this morning.

00:09:53.170 --> 00:09:56.094
And I feel a lot less nervous.

00:09:56.094 --> 00:09:59.282
I feel way more excited than nervous.

00:09:59.282 --> 00:10:00.850
So it's all good.

00:10:00.850 --> 00:10:01.916
It's going to be a great day.

00:10:01.916 --> 00:10:02.749
It's the last day of the summit,

00:10:02.749 --> 00:10:05.416
so it's going to be a fabulous day.

00:10:10.035 --> 00:10:12.748
All right, just got out of
the keynote with Rick Mercer.

00:10:12.748 --> 00:10:14.507
I'm going to head over
to the mentor lounge.

00:10:14.507 --> 00:10:18.356
I think Evan's already
here, so let me go find him.

00:10:18.356 --> 00:10:21.106
(dramatic music)

00:10:22.135 --> 00:10:25.231
All right, day two of Sage Summit done.

00:10:25.231 --> 00:10:29.239
Overall it was a really great experience.

00:10:29.239 --> 00:10:32.971
I haven't been to an
accounting conference before,

00:10:32.971 --> 00:10:37.631
and who knew that it would
actually be a lot of fun.

00:10:37.631 --> 00:10:40.865
There was a keynote with
Rick Mercer this morning.

00:10:40.865 --> 00:10:43.699
To be honest, I didn't know who he was.

00:10:43.699 --> 00:10:45.149
For those of you who don't know,

00:10:45.149 --> 00:10:48.789
he is a Canadian comedian and
his keynote was really good.

00:10:48.789 --> 00:10:52.289
Today I didn't have any coaching sessions,

00:10:54.901 --> 00:10:58.955
but I used the opportunity
to learn from Evan.

00:10:58.955 --> 00:11:01.954
I had some questions for him,
so he guided me through that.

00:11:01.954 --> 00:11:04.771
And I was right beside
him, so I was able to

00:11:04.771 --> 00:11:07.666
kind of sit in and
eavesdrop, a little bit,

00:11:07.666 --> 00:11:10.701
into his sessions and learn from him

00:11:10.701 --> 00:11:13.078
and see what he does, so that way

00:11:13.078 --> 00:11:15.712
I can use some of that method myself

00:11:15.712 --> 00:11:18.577
too and see the way he asked questions,

00:11:18.577 --> 00:11:20.606
looking at his thought
process and all of that.

00:11:20.606 --> 00:11:22.800
Overall it wasn't' a waste, even though

00:11:22.800 --> 00:11:25.543
I was looking forward
to meeting more people.

00:11:25.543 --> 00:11:29.914
But every opportunity is
an opportunity to learn

00:11:29.914 --> 00:11:31.651
So it was great.

00:11:31.651 --> 00:11:33.375
Being part of the Sage Summit

00:11:33.375 --> 00:11:35.858
was such an incredible experience for me.

00:11:35.858 --> 00:11:38.194
Not only did I get to mentor people,

00:11:38.194 --> 00:11:40.296
help them out with their
business and lives,

00:11:40.296 --> 00:11:42.930
I got to watch some great speakers

00:11:42.930 --> 00:11:44.937
deliver their message to us.

00:11:44.937 --> 00:11:46.479
I also met a new friend.

00:11:46.479 --> 00:11:47.525
Her name is Rebecca.

00:11:47.525 --> 00:11:51.014
She shared her favorite
quote with me, which is--

00:11:51.014 --> 00:11:54.307
- Say yes, and figure
the rest out afterwards.

00:11:54.307 --> 00:11:58.284
- Which basically sums up
this entire experience for me.

00:11:58.284 --> 00:12:02.033
When Evan came with a
challenge, I just said yes.

00:12:02.033 --> 00:12:04.896
I had no idea what was expected of me.

00:12:04.896 --> 00:12:06.086
I didn't know the details.

00:12:06.086 --> 00:12:07.336
I didn't know where I needed to be

00:12:07.336 --> 00:12:09.330
at what time, what day, wherever.

00:12:09.330 --> 00:12:12.286
I just said yes and it turns out to be

00:12:12.286 --> 00:12:14.284
one of the best experiences I've had

00:12:14.284 --> 00:12:19.039
in a very long time, and
I'm so glad I said yes.

00:12:19.039 --> 00:12:21.037
For my next challenge I'm going to be

00:12:21.037 --> 00:12:24.054
bringing all of you behind the scenes

00:12:24.054 --> 00:12:26.810
in my mentoring sessions with Evan.

00:12:26.810 --> 00:12:30.863
I learned from Tony Robbins
that success leaves clues.

00:12:30.863 --> 00:12:33.801
If there's something you really
want to be successful at,

00:12:33.801 --> 00:12:35.783
you need to study and mentor under someone

00:12:35.783 --> 00:12:39.349
who has been there and has
been successful consistently.

00:12:39.349 --> 00:12:42.170
And to me, Evan perfectly embodies that

00:12:42.170 --> 00:12:44.469
and is such a great mentor for me.

00:12:44.469 --> 00:12:45.736
The question of the day is,

00:12:45.736 --> 00:12:50.091
what is that one scary
thing that you said yes too

00:12:50.091 --> 00:12:53.825
that turned out to be an
amazing experience for you.

00:12:53.825 --> 00:12:56.231
Thank you so much for watching.

00:12:56.231 --> 00:12:57.817
Your comments and encouragement

00:12:57.817 --> 00:13:01.205
really really gets me excited
and wants me to keep going

00:13:01.205 --> 00:13:03.836
and making all these
videos for all of you.

00:13:03.836 --> 00:13:06.316
I actually have a special
shout out for Jason Bean.

00:13:06.316 --> 00:13:09.782
Jason Bean wrote, "this is so cool."

00:13:09.782 --> 00:13:12.355
Honestly Jason, you've
been there since day one

00:13:12.355 --> 00:13:14.549
and I'm so incredibly honored

00:13:14.549 --> 00:13:17.610
to have you on this journey with me.

00:13:17.610 --> 00:13:19.438
Once again, thank you so much guys.

00:13:19.438 --> 00:13:22.851
I love you all and I'll
see you very very soon.

00:13:22.851 --> 00:13:24.768
(kiss)

